Product Name
NervSync — A Frictionless Nervous System Regulator
________________________________________
1. Problem Statement
Traditional mental health applications require high cognitive effort (typing, reflection, form filling).
When a user is anxious or cognitively overloaded, they are least capable of structured input.
There is a need for:
A zero-friction micro-intervention that detects stress passively and regulates the nervous system through embodied interaction instead of cognitive engagement.
________________________________________
2. Vision
Create a bio-reactive interface that:
•	Detects agitation using device sensors
•	Adapts the UI automatically
•	Induces calm using motor rhythm synchronization
The phone becomes a nervous system mirror, not a diary.
________________________________________
3. Target Audience
Primary:
•	Students experiencing acute stress
•	Hackathon/placement anxiety
•	Exam pressure
Secondary:
•	Urban young adults with high screen dependency
•	Individuals with mild panic episodes
________________________________________
4. Core Innovation
Combines:
Wildcard 1 – Sensor Integration
Using:
•	Accelerometer
•	Touch velocity behavior
•	Tap frequency
Wildcard 2 – Alternative UI
Interaction through:
•	Gravity-based breathing orb
•	Swipe-to-dissolve chaos field
•	Haptic rhythm pacing
No typing. No forms. No surveys.
________________________________________
5. User Experience Flow
5.1 Passive Monitoring (Background State Capture)
System monitors:
•	Sudden repetitive phone movement
•	Shake intensity
•	Rapid tap bursts
•	Touch velocity inconsistencies
________________________________________
5.2 State Detection Logic
State Machine:
•	Calm
•	Mild Stress
•	High Agitation
Trigger Conditions Example:
If:
•	Movement intensity > threshold
•	Tap speed irregularity > baseline
Then:
→ Move to Mild Stress
If:
•	Continuous high acceleration spikes
Then:
→ High Agitation
________________________________________
5.3 Intervention Trigger
When stress state detected:
•	UI transitions automatically
•	Colors soften
•	Animations slow
•	Haptics begin guided pacing
No notification needed.
________________________________________
6. Core Features (MVP Scope)
Feature 1: Sensor Monitoring Engine
Description:
Continuously gathers accelerometer and gesture data.
Requirement:
•	Process 60Hz accelerometer data
•	Calculate delta movement over 3-second windows
•	Compute tap speed per 5 seconds
Output:
Stress score (0–100)
________________________________________
Feature 2: Nervous System State Engine
Description:
Rule-based classification engine.
Inputs:
•	Movement intensity
•	Gesture velocity
•	Tap rate
Output:
Current emotional state
________________________________________
Feature 3: Gravity Breathing Orb (Primary Intervention)
Description:
A floating orb moves in vertical sinusoidal motion.
User must drag finger to follow.
System:
•	Slows motion gradually
•	Matches 4-6 breathing rhythm
•	Provides haptic pulse during inhale/exhale
Objective:
Force motor synchronization → regulate breath.
________________________________________
Feature 4: Chaos Dissolve Mode (High Stress Mode)
Description:
Screen fills with chaotic particles.
User must swipe slowly to dissolve them.
Only slow gestures reduce particle speed.
Encourages:
Intentional slowing of movement.
________________________________________
Feature 5: Adaptive UI Shift
Depending on stress level:
Calm:
•	Neutral color palette
•	Subtle animations
Mild Stress:
•	Slightly slower UI animations
•	Gentle blur reduction
High Stress:
•	Full regulation mode
•	Orb dominant full screen
•	Reduced visual clutter
________________________________________
7. Non-Functional Requirements
•	Response latency < 300ms
•	Intervention trigger time < 3 seconds
•	Must function offline
•	No login required
•	No stored personal data
________________________________________
8. Technical Stack
Recommended:
•	Expo + React Native
•	expo-sensors
•	expo-haptics
•	react-native-reanimated
•	react-native-gesture-handler
Backend:
Not required for MVP (local processing).
________________________________________
9. System Architecture
Sensor Layer
↓
Signal Processing Layer
↓
State Classification Engine
↓
Intervention Controller
↓
UI + Haptic Output
________________________________________
10. Success Metrics
For hackathon demo:
•	Sensor activity visibly influences UI
•	Real-time state switching demonstrated
•	Breathing orb slows user interaction
•	No text inputs used
________________________________________
11. Risks & Mitigation
Risk: Sensor noise
Mitigation: Use moving average smoothing
Risk: Demo failure due to low movement
Mitigation: Manual agitation simulation mode for demo
Risk: Overengineering in 7 hours
Mitigation: Keep state engine rule-based
________________________________________
12. Out of Scope (For MVP)
•	AI stress prediction
•	Cloud data sync
•	Clinical diagnostics
•	User history tracking
________________________________________
13. Demo Script Strategy
During presentation:
1.	Shake phone rapidly
2.	Show UI transition
3.	Open gravity orb
4.	Demonstrate haptic inhale/exhale sync
5.	Explain how motor rhythm entrains breath
Do not focus on UI beauty.
Focus on physiological loop.
________________________________________
14. Why This Is 60% Novel
•	Doesn’t ask user to describe emotions
•	Doesn’t rely on chatbot
•	Uses behavioral biometrics
•	Regulates body rhythm indirectly
•	Two wildcards integrated seamlessly
________________________________________
15. Team Responsibility Breakdown
Member 1:
Sensor ingestion + stress score calculation
Member 2:
State engine + logic transitions
Member 3:
Breathing orb animation + gestures
Member 4:
UI polish + documentation + testing + demo narrative

